    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on exploiting soft matchups to manufacture speed and efficiency, headlined by **Corbin Carroll** (85.94) and **James Wood** (76.28). **Corbin Carroll** is our premier play, benefiting from a high-run-environment park and a favorable matchup against Lorenzen; his elite sprint speed gives him a massive ceiling in our scarcity-driven 5x5 format. Similarly, **James Wood** is in a prime position to produce, as his leadoff status (+10%) and the soft xERA of his opposing starter create a high-floor opportunity to generate runs and steals. We are also leaning heavily into the wheels of **Brice Turang** (74.03), whose matchup against a slower-to-the-plate starter elevates his stolen base probability, further bolstering his strong daily efficiency score.\n\nThe decision to field **Mickey Moniak** (73.50) over **Kyle Karros** (44.89) was the most significant deliberation in today\u2019s build. While **Kyle Karros** benefits from a hitter-friendly park, his low batting order position (-6%) and inferior matchup profile ultimately relegated him to the bench. In contrast, **Mickey Moniak** secures a starting spot thanks to an aggressive +14% dynamic platoon boost and a prominent #2 spot in the lineup, making him a superior choice for run and RBI accumulation. We are also monitoring the performance of **Dalton Rushing** and **Gabriel Moreno**, both of whom are projected for solid, if unspectacular, production today. While **Cole Young** (48.10) sits at the low end of our starting threshold due to a slight park disadvantage, his inclusion is necessary to maintain our positional coverage; he remains a player to watch for early-game pull, though he is currently our most volatile offensive piece.",
